          "Marius followed the barbarians and at Aquae Sextiae pitched camp on a height poorly supplied with water. On the first day servants and soldiers who went down to the river for water clashed with the Ambrones, who were bathing and feasting; the Ligurian auxiliaries began the fight, and the Romans drove them beyond the river (19–20).\n\n"
